# Default .gitignore for a new project.
#
# Covers the broad, safe cases only. Add project-specific rules at the bottom.
# For a Unity project, prefer `unity vcs doctor --fix`, which generates the full
# Unity-specific file from the editor's own knowledge - see docs.
#
# A note worth remembering: Git cannot track an EMPTY folder. An empty directory
# never appears on the remote and is not created by a clone. Put a .gitkeep or a
# README.md inside any folder that must exist.

# --- editor and OS cruft ---------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.vs/
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# --- scratch and backups ---------------------------------------------------
# (the whole point of this setup is that these should not be needed)
*.bak
*.orig
*.tmp
*.temp
_scratch/
tmp/

# --- logs ------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/

# --- secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Never commit credentials.
.env
.env.local
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# --- project-specific ------------------------------------------------------
# Add yours below.
